@0    = ~Oh, come on. She's interested in women, not some layabout off the street with nothing to offer.~
@1    = ~Way she's been acting with me, I'm not so sure about that.~
@2    = ~You're deluding yourself. Trust me. You're barking up the wrong tree.~
@3    = ~By Akadia, I can't take this any longer!~
@4    = ~Ooh, are you having visions from the gods again?~
@5    = ~You stay out of this. <CHARNAME>, Faren's been acting very oddly lately. I think he has some idea that he can muscle in on us.~
@6    = ~You know how men are. They see a couple of women getting close and they think they can indulge in some ridiculous fantasy. As if they're the gods' gift to us.~
@7    = ~Chloe, you're thinking too much of yourself. You know what? If I wanted to go with two women, it would definitely not be with you.~
@8    = ~<CHARNAME>, you see how he is. Please, let him know where things stand.~
@9    = ~Faren, I think of you as a friend, but I don't feel anything more.~
@10   = ~Chloe, of course I want you more than Faren. I don't feel anything for him.~
@11   = ~You're wrong, Chloe -- I do like Faren that way.~
@12   = ~Oh. Well. Fair enough, then.~
@13   = ~Finally! I'm just glad we could clear that up.~
@14   = ~You're making a mistake, <CHARNAME>. This man has nothing to offer you -- nothing.~
@15   = ~Oh, well. Maybe we'll leave it to her to decide that, yeah?~
@16   = ~Must you ogle every female we see, Faren? It's getting embarrassing.~
@17   = ~No harm in looking, is there? Long as they don't mind.~
@18   = ~None of them have any reason to be interested in you, and yet you continue to try. What's the point?~
@19   = ~Hey, there's reasons for them to be interested in me. Lots of reasons.~
@20   = ~Such as?~
@21   = ~Smiling, girls like smiling. You should try it sometime. Mostly it's the hair, though. Can't lie.~
@22   = ~That's ridiculous. Anyway, just keep your eyes to yourself.~
@23   = ~Hey, well, it looks like it's working with a certain woman of our acquaintance, doesn't it?~
@24   = ~I can't imagine why. Anyway, just keep your eyes to yourself.~
@25   = ~So, you have Chult blood, do you? Do you know anything of your ancestors?~
@26   = ~Wouldn't know anything about Chult. My family's Trademeet born and bred.~
@27   = ~Really? That's a pity. It's good to know where you come from.~
@28   = ~I know where I come from, and it's none of your damn business.~
@29   = ~Touched a nerve, have I? Well, isn't that interesting?~
@30   = ~Stop shivering, Faren, for Lathander's sake. You're distracting me.~
@31   = ~I hate Amn - above and below. Wish I could head over to Luskan again. Now, that's a nice place to be.~
@32   = ~Then why not go there again, and save the rest of us your whining?~
